cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this knowledge base or the mijhar engine, please cite it."
title: "Unified AI Text Detection Knowledge Base + mijhar evidence engine"
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-19"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sharar"
    given-names: "Elias"
    affiliation: "bio-colab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bio-colab/ai-text-detection"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - AI text detection
  - stylometry
  - academic integrity
  - Arabic NLP
abstract: >
  A bilingual (Arabic/English) open knowledge base of 153 unique documented
  signals for investigating AI-generated text, eight critical-limitation
  dossiers (false positives on non-native writers, theoretical impossibility,
  Arabic detection, mixed texts, external evidence, commercial claims,
  calibration, signal obsolescence), a verified key-papers bibliography, and
  mijhar: a deterministic, stdlib-only evidence scanner that collects
  human-verifiable excerpts and never outputs a verdict.
